Subject: Open the start page when started with no URL

Application::newInstance() opens a page only for a URL on the command
line, so a launch from the menu, whose Exec is `khelpcenter %u` with no
URL, shows an empty content pane until a page is picked. With no URL,
call MainWindow::openUrl() with an empty URL, which shows the start page,
as the Table of Contents entry and the Home action do. A URL given on the
command line is opened as before.

--- a/application.cpp
+++ b/application.cpp
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@
     if (!urls.isEmpty()) {
         const QUrl url = QUrl::fromUserInput(urls.at(0), QDir::currentPath());
         mMainWindow->openUrl(url);
+    } else {
+        mMainWindow->openUrl(QUrl());
     }
 }
 
